    "slot_value": "POS-impacting batch updates should pause or be blocked if they would change items that are actively being sold or counted, including when there is an open sales session, a live checkout in progress, or a critical inventory count on those items. Sensitive or high-impact changes should also trigger alerts sooner and usually have a shorter tolerance for waiting. Anything that affects sellable stock in a busy department or touches high-value or unique items should notify staff quickly if it is held up, while lower-risk housekeeping changes can wait longer. A simple note update is less urgent than anything that changes quantity, availability, or POS-facing stock.",
